^{:go/end 505} (go/func encodeI1Tsz "encodeI1Tsz is the implementation of the following encoding logic:\nIs the immediate index, in the range 0 to one less than the number of elements in 128 bits, encoded in \"i1:tsz\".\nbit range mappings:\ni1: [20:21)\ntsz: [16:20)\nNote:\n\n\tarr is the arrangement.\n\tThis encoding is aligned to the high bit of the box, according to the spec.\n" [^uint32 v ^uint32 arr] :results [uint32 bool]
  (switch arr
    (case [ARNG_B]
      (when (> v 15)
        (return 0 false))

      (return (<< v 17) true))
    (case [ARNG_H]
      (when (> v 7)
        (return 0 false))

      (return (<< v 18) true))
    (case [ARNG_S]
      (when (> v 3)
        (return 0 false))

      (return (<< v 19) true))
    (case [ARNG_D]
      (when (> v 1)
        (return 0 false))

      (return (<< v 20) true))
    (case [ARNG_Q]
      (when (> v 0)
        (return 0 false))

      (return 0 true))
    (default
      (return 0 false))))












